{"id":"msk-pharmacology","system":"Musculoskeletal, Skin & Connective Tissue","subject":"Pharmacology","pages":[495,498],"rounds":[{"t":"Arachidonic acid pathways, acetaminophen, aspirin, and celecoxib","q":[{"s":"Glucocorticoids reduce production of both prostaglandins and leukotrienes by inhibiting which enzyme?","o":["5-lipoxygenase","Phospholipase A2","Cyclooxygenase-1 only","Xanthine oxidase","Thromboxane synthase"],"e":["Wrong. Zileuton.","Correct. Also via NF-κB/IκB effects.","Wrong. NSAIDs.","Wrong. Allopurinol.","Wrong. Not correct."],"a":1,"p":"495","k":"Arachidonic acid pathways"},{"s":"Zileuton inhibits which enzyme?","o":["COX-2","5-lipoxygenase","Cyclooxygenase-1","Phospholipase A2","Prostacyclin synthase"],"e":["Wrong. Celecoxib.","Correct. Blocks leukotriene synthesis.","Wrong. NSAIDs.","Wrong. Glucocorticoids.","Wrong. Not correct."],"a":1,"p":"495","k":"Arachidonic acid pathways"},{"s":"Montelukast and zafirlukast act by:","o":["Inhibiting 5-lipoxygenase","Inhibiting COX","Blocking H1 receptors","Inhibiting phospholipase A2","Blocking leukotriene receptors"],"e":["Wrong. Zileuton.","Wrong. NSAIDs.","Wrong. Antihistamines.","Wrong. Glucocorticoids.","Correct."],"a":4,"p":"495","k":"Arachidonic acid pathways"},{"s":"Which leukotriene is a neutrophil chemotactic agent?","o":["LTC4","LTD4","PGI2","LTB4","LTE4"],"e":["Wrong. Bronchoconstriction.","Wrong. Bronchoconstriction.","Wrong. Not a leukotriene.","Correct. \"Neutrophils arrive B4 others.\"","Wrong. Bronchoconstriction."],"a":3,"p":"495","k":"Arachidonic acid pathways"},{"s":"Which eicosanoid inhibits platelet aggregation and causes vasodilation?","o":["LTB4","PGI2 (prostacyclin)","PGF2α","TXA2","LTC4"],"e":["Wrong. Chemotaxis.","Correct. \"Platelet-Gathering Inhibitor.\"","Wrong. Uterine contraction.","Wrong. Opposite.","Wrong. Bronchoconstriction."],"a":1,"p":"495","k":"Arachidonic acid pathways"},{"s":"Epoprostenol is an analog of which eicosanoid, used for pulmonary hypertension?","o":["PGE2",